[{"url": "https://www.dycomind.com/news-releases/news-release-details/dycom-industries-reports-first-quarter-fiscal-2026-results", "content": "Dycom Industries Reports First Quarter Fiscal 2026 Results\n\nOrganic revenue growth of 15.7% and net income of $90.0 million in the first quarter\nBacklog increased to $9.37 billion\n\nWEST PALM BEACH, Fla., November 20, 2024 /PRNewswire/ -- Dycom Industries, Inc. (NYSE: DY) reported results for its first fiscal quarter ended October 26, 2024. For the first fiscal quarter ended October 26, 2024, contract revenues were $1.188 billion, an increase of 18.0% as compared to contract revenues of $1.007 billion for the first fiscal quarter ended October 28, 2023. Organic revenue growth was 15.7%.\n\nDycom currently operates under several subsidiary companies across the U.S. The Company's backlog increased to $9.37 billion, with $4.70 billion expected to be completed in the next twelve months.\n\n\"We had a strong first quarter driven by continued robust customer spending on wireless and wireline projects. The increased activity reflects customers focused on accelerating deployment of broadband, fiber, and 5G networks,\" said Steven Nielsen, President and CEO. \"Our customers' forward expectations remain strong, with major carriers and broadband customers focused on multi-year deployments.\"\n\n\"Our first quarter reflects strong performance, solid execution, and continued customer confidence in our capabilities,\" said Drew DeFerrari, Senior Vice President and CFO. \"We are well positioned to capitalize on favorable industry trends as customers execute their long-term capital spending programs.\"\n\nThe Company's total liquidity as of October 26, 2024 was $879.4 million.\n\nFor the full fiscal year 2025, the Company currently provides the following guidance:\n\nContract revenues of $4.850 to $4.900 billion\nAdjusted EBITDA margins of approximately 13%\n\nDycom provides engineering, design, construction, maintenance and installation services throughout the United States, primarily to:\n\nTelecom operators (AT&T, Verizon, Comcast, and others)\nCable operators\nUnderground facility locating businesses\nElectrical and gas utilities\n\nFiscal Year 2025 full year guidance was renegotiated. Revenue of $4.85 billion to $4.900 billion was provided.\n\nFor further information contact:\n\nSteven Nielsen, President and CEO\nDrew DeFerrari, Senior Vice President and CFO\nPhone: (561) 627-7171", "date": ""}]
</tool_response>

